# Rewritten for tone
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtEngineering = engineering jumpskirt
    .desc = Lightly dusted with soot and debris from long repair jobs.

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtHoP = head of personnel's jumpskirt
    .desc = You're the person in charge of the uniforms. If your own uniform was anything less than exceptional, it'd be a disgrace!

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtBrigmedic = combat medic jumpskirt
    .desc = This uniform is issued to qualified personnel who have been trained. Infamously hard to keep clean.

# Cargo -> Logistics
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtCargo = cargo tech jumpskirt
    .desc = A sturdy jumpskirt, issued to members of the Logistics department.

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtQM = logistics officer's jumpskirt
    .desc = 'What can brown do for you?'

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtQMTurtleneck = logistics officer's turtleneck
    .desc = A sharp turtleneck made for the hardy work environment of supply.

# Specific name to more generic ones
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtJanimaid = maid uniform
    .desc = For professionals, not the posers.

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtJanimaidmini = maid uniform with miniskirt
    .desc = Elite service, not some candy wrappers.

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtLawyerRed = red suitskirt
    .desc = A flashy red suitskirt worn by lawyers and show-offs.

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtLawyerBlue = blue suitskirt
    .desc = A flashy blue suitskirt worn by lawyers and show-offs.

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtLawyerBlack = black suitskirt
    .desc = A subtle black suitskirt worn by lawyers and gangsters.

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtLawyerPurple = purple suitskirt
    .desc = A stylish purple piece worn by lawyers and show people.

# Lore rewrites
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtSyndieFormalDress = syndicate formal dress
    .desc = The upper echelons of Syndicate bureaucracy are all about making the right impression, which always starts with the right outfit. This one reads something like "I'm in charge here."

ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtSecGrey = grey security jumpskirt
    .desc = A tactical relic of years past before Cybersun decided it was cheaper to tell SyndComm to dye the suits red instead of washing out the blood.
